x86_64-linux  this case includes <cassert>, a header cxx1 provides and clang does not on the cross targets - so clang cannot compile it for x86_64-linux or x86_64-windows (file not found), and on arm64-darwin it folds the constant assert condition and emits no __assert_rtn call where cxx1 keeps one. The names comparison is a library difference, not an ABI one. What this case is about - <cassert> re-read on a second include compiles, its extern "C" balancing on every pass - is checked by run.sh on all three machines.
